        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mia Hansen-Løve, Isabelle Huppert, Lola Créton\n- Films: Goodbye First Love, Things to Come, Something in the Air\n- Events: 66th Berlin International Film Festival\n- Roles: director, actor, philosophy professor\n\nFacts:\n- Goodbye First Love is a 2011 Franco-German film directed by Mia Hansen-Løve.\n- Lola Créton is known for her lead role in Goodbye First Love.\n- Lola Créton is also known for her lead role in Something in the Air (2012).\n- In 2016, Things to Come starred Isabelle Huppert as middle-aged philosophy professor Nathalie Chazeaux, whose life is undergoing a series of separations.\n- In 2016, Mia Hansen-Løve won the Silver Bear for Best Director for Things to Come at the 66th Berlin International Film Festival.",
